OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Diagnostics/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the
`TeslaSync/` group only holds the legacy `feature-views`/`shared-surfaces`/`*-widgets`
surfaces). The repo's real, compiled, canonical P7-page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Category>/**` — where every shipped P7 page lives
(`Sources/Features/Analytics/Statistics*`, `Sources/Features/Admin/ApiPlayground*`, …) and
which `project.yml` already lists as the `Sources` source path (createIntermediateGroups).
The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Diagnostics/**`, the faithful
equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Diagnostics`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation the sibling ApiPlayground / DiskForecast logs recorded; it is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web page is reachable at `/analytics/anomalies` (canonical) and
`/anomaly-detection` (web `App.tsx` both routes -> AnomalyDashboard). The `.analytics`
AppRoute is already owned by Fleet Analytics / Statistics. The page lives under
`features/diagnostics` and is the sole `page:diagnostics/*` manifest unit, so it hosts on
the previously-unregistered `.diagnostics` AppRoute (System/Operations sidebar entry,
icon "stethoscope"). `AppRouteParser.aliases` gains `/analytics/anomalies -> .diagnostics`
and `/anomaly-detection -> .diagnostics` so both web deep links resolve. Recorded per
covenant #9.

